docs/scratch/arrival-sliceC/explorers/e4-cas-token.json:1:{"conversation_id":"837c9494-60a9-4dc4-aca6-9b92e9501ce1","status":"SUCCESS","response":"### 1. CAS Token \u0026 Lineage Predicate Code\n\n[libs/engine/src/engine/sqlite_store.py:1448-1493](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/libs/engine/src/engine/sqlite_store.py#L1448-L1493)\n\n```python\n    def _declaration_head_in_txn(\n        self, conn: Any, lineage_id: str\n    ) -\u003e tuple[int, str] | None:\n        \"\"\"The ``(rowid, id)`` of the newest self-lineage declaration row.\n\n        Genesis included; foreign-lineage ``_decl.*`` rows excluded (their\n        payload stamps a different lineage). This is the CAS token\n        ``absorb_edit`` compares ``expected_head`` against — receipt-ordered\n        by rowid, the same axis the resolver folds on.\n        \"\"\"\n        best: tuple[int, str] | None = None\n        rows = conn.execute(\n            \"SELECT id, kind, rowid, payload FROM facts WHERE kind GLOB '_decl.*'\"\n        ).fetchall()\n        for fact_id, kind, rowid, payload_text in rows:\n            if fact_id == lineage_id:\n                pass  # own genesis participates\n            else:\n                try:\n                    payload = json.loads(payload_text)\n                except (json.JSONDecodeError, TypeError):\n                    continue\n                if payload.get(\"lineage\") != lineage_id:\n                    continue\n            candidate = (rowid, fact_id)\n            if best is None or candidate \u003e best:\n                best = candidate\n        return best\n\n    def declaration_head(self) -\u003e tuple[int, str] | None:\n        \"\"\"Public read of the self-lineage declaration head (CAS token).\n\n        Captured by the CLI at diff time and passed back as ``absorb_edit``'s\n        ``expected_head`` so a concurrent re-absorb between diff and apply is\n        refused instead of silently interleaved. None when the lineage is not\n        open (or unmarked-ambiguous — the write ceremony will refuse anyway).\n        \"\"\"\n        self._ensure_meta_table()\n        conn = self._conn\n        try:\n            lineage = self._own_lineage_in_txn(conn)\n        except AmbiguousGenesis:\n            return None\n        if lineage is None:\n            return None\n        return self._declaration_head_in_txn(conn, lineage)\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Every Site Producing, Parsing, or Comparing the CAS Token\n\n#### Production Sites (`declaration_head()` / `_declaration_head_in_txn()`)\n- [libs/engine/src/engine/sqlite_store.py:1448-1475](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/libs/engine/src/engine/sqlite_store.py#L1448-L1475) — Produces `(rowid, fact_id)` tuple:\n  ```python\n              candidate = (rowid, fact_id)\n              if best is None or candidate \u003e best:\n                  best = candidate\n          return best\n  ```\n- [libs/engine/src/engine/sqlite_store.py:1477-1493](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/libs/engine/src/engine/sqlite_store.py#L1477-L1493) — Public reader returning `tuple[int, str] | None`:\n  ```python\n      def declaration_head(self) -\u003e tuple[int, str] | None:\n  ...\n          return self._declaration_head_in_txn(conn, lineage)\n  ```\n- [libs/engine/src/engine/ceremony.py:382](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/libs/engine/src/engine/ceremony.py#L382) — Captures token during update planning:\n  ```python\n          expected_head = store.declaration_head()\n  ```\n- [apps/loops/src/loops/commands/store.py:1257](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/apps/loops/src/loops/commands/store.py#L1257) — Captures token during CLI absorb diff:\n  ```python\n          expected_head = store.declaration_head()\n  ```\n\n#### Parsing / Serialization Sites\n- [libs/engine/src/engine/ceremony.py:432-434](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/libs/engine/src/engine/ceremony.py#L432-L434) — Serializes `expected_head` into intent record `old_decl_head` list:\n  ```python\n          \"old_decl_head\": list(preview.expected_head)\n          if preview.expected_head\n          else None,\n  ```\n\n#### Comparison \u0026 Enforcement Sites\n- [libs/engine/src/engine/sqlite_store.py:1098-1106](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/libs/engine/src/engine/sqlite_store.py#L1098-L1106) — Validates `expected_head` inside transaction CAS check:\n  ```python\n                  if expected_head is not None:\n                      head = self._declaration_head_in_txn(conn, lineage_id)\n                      if head != tuple(expected_head):\n                          raise StaleDeclarationHead(\n                              f\"declaration head moved: expected {expected_head}, \"\n                              f\"store is at {head} — another edit landed since \"\n                              \"the diff was computed; re-run absorb against the \"\n                              \"current head\"\n                          )\n  ```\n\n#### Invocation / Forwarding Sites\n- [libs/engine/src/engine/ceremony.py:606-612](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/libs/engine/src/engine/ceremony.py#L606-L612) — Passes token to store in update ceremony:\n  ```python\n          def ceremony() -\u003e dict[str, Any]:\n              return store.absorb_edit(\n                  list(preview.changes),\n                  observer=observer,\n                  origin=\"\",\n                  fact_signer=fact_signer,\n                  expected_head=preview.expected_head,\n              )\n  ```\n- [apps/loops/src/loops/commands/store.py:1356-1362](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/apps/loops/src/loops/commands/store.py#L1356-L1362) — Passes token from CLI command:\n  ```python\n              store.absorb_edit(\n                  changes,\n                  observer=observer,\n                  origin=\"\",\n                  fact_signer=fact_signer_for(target_path),\n                  expected_head=expected_head,\n              )\n  ```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Persisted Intent Record in `ceremony.py`\n\n**Full path**: `libs/engine/src/engine/ceremony.py` (absolute: `/Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/libs/engine/src/engine/ceremony.py`)  \n[libs/engine/src/engine/ceremony.py:423-441](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/libs/engine/src/engine/ceremony.py#L423-L441)\n\n```python\ndef _write_intent(preview: DeclarationUpdatePreview, observer: str) -\u003e Path:\n    intent = {\n        \"v\": _INTENT_VERSION,\n        \"mode\": preview.mode,\n        \"vertex_path\": str(preview.vertex_path),\n        \"canonical_path\": str(preview.canonical_path),\n        \"created_ts\": datetime.now(UTC).timestamp(),\n        \"observer\": observer,\n        \"old_status\": preview.declaration_status,\n        \"old_decl_head\": list(preview.expected_head)\n        if preview.expected_head\n        else None,\n        \"old_store_fingerprint\": preview.old_store_fingerprint,\n        \"lineage\": preview.generation.get(\"lineage\"),\n        \"proposed_fingerprint\": preview.proposed_fingerprint,\n        \"proposed_documents\": list(preview.documents),\n        \"proposed_text\": preview.proposed_text,\n    }\n    path = intent_path_for(preview.vertex_path)\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. CAS Token Grammar / Format\n\nThe CAS token is not formatted as a string via f-strings or join. It is constructed and returned as a 2-tuple `(rowid, fact_id)` where `rowid` is an `int` and `fact_id` is a `str` (the declaration event fact ID / ULID):\n\n- Construction: [libs/engine/src/engine/sqlite_store.py:1472](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/libs/engine/src/engine/sqlite_store.py#L1472)\n  ```python\n              candidate = (rowid, fact_id)\n  ```\n- Type signature: [libs/engine/src/engine/sqlite_store.py:1450](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/libs/engine/src/engine/sqlite_store.py#L1450) and [libs/engine/src/engine/sqlite_store.py:1477](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/libs/engine/src/engine/sqlite_store.py#L1477)\n  ```python\n  tuple[int, str] | None\n  ```\n- JSON serialization format: In intent records, it is serialized as a 2-element JSON list `[rowid, fact_id]` or `null`: [libs/engine/src/engine/ceremony.py:432-434](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/libs/engine/src/engine/ceremony.py#L432-L434)\n  ```python\n        \"old_decl_head\": list(preview.expected_head)\n        if preview.expected_head\n        else None,\n  ```\n\n---\n\n### 5. Tests Referencing the CAS Token or Intent Record\n\n#### CAS Token Tests\n- [libs/engine/tests/test_absorb_edit.py:191-220](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/libs/engine/tests/test_absorb_edit.py#L191-L220): `test_stale_expected_head_refuses`\n- [libs/engine/tests/test_absorb_edit.py:221-287](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/libs/engine/tests/test_absorb_edit.py#L221-L287): `test_cas_token_rides_the_receipt_axis`\n- [libs/engine/tests/test_jsonl_ceremonies.py:207-222](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/libs/engine/tests/test_jsonl_ceremonies.py#L207-L222): `test_stale_head_refuses_with_log_byte_identical`\n- [libs/engine/tests/test_jsonl_ceremonies.py:224-255](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/libs/engine/tests/test_jsonl_ceremonies.py#L224-L255): `test_stale_head_allows_lawful_pre_cas_index_catch_up`\n- [libs/engine/tests/test_ceremony_orchestration.py:177-203](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/libs/engine/tests/test_ceremony_orchestration.py#L177-L203): `test_stale_preview_refuses_log_byte_identical_file_untouched`\n- [libs/engine/tests/test_ceremony_orchestration.py:205-211](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/libs/engine/tests/test_ceremony_orchestration.py#L205-L211): `test_stale_genesis_preview_refuses`\n\n#### Intent Record Tests\n- [libs/engine/tests/test_ceremony_orchestration.py:504-522](file:///Users/kayge