:\n  - [`libs/engine/tests/test_handle_incremental.py:110-120`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/libs/engine/tests/test_handle_incremental.py#L110-L120): `test_incremental_fold_equals_cold_fold_at_every_position`\n  - [`libs/engine/tests/test_handle_incremental.py:123-142`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/libs/engine/tests/test_handle_incremental.py#L123-L142): `test_multi_fact_batches_fold_in_place_correctly`\n  - [`libs/engine/tests/test_handle_incremental.py:144-157`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/libs/engine/tests/test_handle_incremental.py#L144-L157): `test_backdated_append_still_wins_the_upsert_incrementally`\n  - [`libs/engine/tests/test_handle_incremental.py:164-173`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/libs/engine/tests/test_handle_incremental.py#L164-L173): `test_warm_refresh_reports_checkpoint_suffix_after_seeding`\n  - [`libs/engine/tests/test_handle_incremental.py:175-190`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/libs/engine/tests/test_handle_incremental.py#L175-L190): `test_force_reports_full_and_drops_the_checkpoint`\n  - [`libs/engine/tests/test_handle_incremental.py:192-206`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/libs/engine/tests/test_handle_incremental.py#L192-L206): `test_control_fact_forces_full_never_folds_across_an_epoch`\n  - [`libs/engine/tests/test_handle_incremental.py:208-221`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/libs/engine/tests/test_handle_incremental.py#L208-L221): `test_tick_only_refresh_is_unchanged`\n  - [`libs/engine/tests/test_handle_incremental.py:228-247`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/libs/engine/tests/test_handle_incremental.py#L228-L247): `test_diff_folds_rows_identical_on_both_paths`\n  - [`libs/engine/tests/test_handle_bench.py:78-99`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/libs/engine/tests/test_handle_bench.py#L78-L99): `test_refresh_after_one_append_under_gate_at_10k`\n- **Spec `replay_from` tests (the underlying fold-in-place primitive)**:\n  - [`libs/atoms/tests/test_replay.py:100-139`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/libs/atoms/tests/test_replay.py#L100-L139): `TestSpecReplayFrom` (`test_suffix_replay_equals_whole_replay_at_every_split`, `test_input_state_is_not_mutated`)\n\n---\n\n### 3. Rule 17\n\n- **Test verbatim**: [`tests/architecture/test_rule_17_fold_order_prose_is_receipt_order.py:203-232`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/tests/architecture/test_rule_17_fold_order_prose_is_receipt_order.py#L203-L232)\n```python\ndef test_fold_order_prose_is_receipt_order():\n    \"\"\"No shipped prose claims `(ts, id)` orders the fold.\n\n    Fold replay order is receipt order (``rowid``); ``(ts, id)`` is a read lens\n    (docs/RECEIPT_ORDER_FOLD.md). Comments, docstrings, and spec/docs\n    Markdown that still describe the old total order are not cosmetic: they are\n    how the superseded model gets rebuilt in the next reader's head, and they\n    are invisible to every behavioral test in the repo.\n\n    A new hit means one of two things, and the failure message says which to\n    pick. Relabel the site (say \"read lens\", say what it projects, or state the\n    rule it is denying) — that is the fix in almost every case. Or, if the site\n    is genuinely lens and cannot be phrased without the pattern, add an\n    allowlist entry with a comment saying WHY it is lens. The allowlist may\n    only shrink over time; each addition is a small permanent debt.\n    \"\"\"\n    found = _found_claims()\n    unexpected = sorted((p, ln) for p, ln in found if not _allowed(p, ln))\n\n    assert not unexpected, (\n        \"Prose claiming `(ts, id)` / ts-ordering as FOLD or REPLAY order \"\n        \"(fold order is receipt order — rowid; see \"\n        \"docs/RECEIPT_ORDER_FOLD.md):\\n\"\n        + \"\\n\".join(f\"  {p}: {ln[:120]}\" for p, ln in unexpected)\n        + \"\\n\\nFix by RELABELLING the site as a read lens (preferred), or — if \"\n        \"it truly is a lens and cannot avoid the pattern — add a (path, \"\n        \"marker) entry to _ALLOWLIST in this file with a comment saying why. \"\n        \"The allowlist is shrink-only.\"\n    )\n```\n\n- **File-selection code**: [`tests/architecture/test_rule_17_fold_order_prose_is_receipt_order.py:147-179`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/tests/architecture/test_rule_17_fold_order_prose_is_receipt_order.py#L147-L179)\n```python\ndef _scan_targets() -\u003e list:\n    \"\"\"Every shipped-prose file this rule judges.\n\n    Derived from the filesystem, never hand-enumerated (docs/RATCHETS.md): a\n    hand-written list is a silent pass for every lib, app, and doc added after\n    it was written.\n    \"\"\"\n    targets: list = []\n    for production in (\"libs\", \"apps\"):\n        base = REPO_ROOT / production\n        if not base.is_dir():\n            continue\n        for package in sorted(base.iterdir()):\n            src = package / \"src\"\n            if src.is_dir():\n                targets.extend(src.rglob(\"*.py\"))\n    for docs_root in (\"spec\", \"docs\"):\n        base = REPO_ROOT / docs_root\n        if base.is_dir():\n            targets.extend(base.rglob(\"*.md\"))\n    # Conformance generators: their CASE descriptions are copied verbatim into\n    # the vectors, which are normative artifacts other implementations read.\n    generators = REPO_ROOT / \"spec\" / \"conformance\"\n    if generators.is_dir():\n        targets.extend(sorted(generators.glob(\"generate_*.py\")))\n    return [\n        p\n        for p in sorted(set(targets))\n        if \"mutants\" not in p.parts\n        and \"__pycache__\" not in p.parts\n        and \".venv\" not in p.parts\n    ]\n```\n\n- **File-selection method**: The file-selection code uses a **filesystem walk** (`Path.rglob`, `Path.glob`, and `Path.iterdir`), not `git ls-files`.\n- **Exclusion list and `docs/scratch`**: `docs/scratch` is **absent** from any exclusion list. The exclusion filter on lines 175–177 excludes only `\"mutants\"`, `\"__pycache__\"`, and `\".venv\"`:\n```python\n174:     return [\n175:         p\n176:         for p in sorted(set(targets))\n177:         if \"mutants\" not in p.parts\n178:         and \"__pycache__\" not in p.parts\n179:         and \".venv\" not in p.parts\n180:     ]\n```\nBecause `base = REPO_ROOT / \"docs\"` walks `base.rglob(\"*.md\")`, all Markdown files under `docs/scratch/` are included in the scan.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Architecture Test Suite Layout\n\n- [`tests/architecture/test_rule_01_apps_no_store_reader.py:1`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/tests/architecture/test_rule_01_apps_no_store_reader.py#L1): `\"\"\"Rule 1: Apps don't import StoreReader.\"\"\"`\n- [`tests/architecture/test_rule_02_apps_no_raw_sqlite.py:1`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/tests/architecture/test_rule_02_apps_no_raw_sqlite.py#L1): `\"\"\"Rule 2: Apps don't access raw database connections.\"\"\"`\n- [`tests/architecture/test_rule_03_libs_dont_import_apps.py:1`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/tests/architecture/test_rule_03_libs_dont_import_apps.py#L1): `\"\"\"Rule 3: Libs don't import from apps.\"\"\"`\n- [`tests/architecture/test_rule_04_lib_dependency_dag.py:1`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/tests/architecture/test_rule_04_lib_dependency_dag.py#L1): `\"\"\"Rule 4: Lib dependency DAG.\"\"\"`\n- [`tests/architecture/test_rule_05_lib_dataclasses_frozen.py:1`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/tests/architecture/test_rule_05_lib_dataclasses_frozen.py#L1): `\"\"\"Rule 5: Lib dataclasses must be frozen.\"\"\"`\n- [`tests/architecture/test_rule_06_atoms_stdlib_only.py:1`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/tests/architecture/test_rule_06_atoms_stdlib_only.py#L1): `\"\"\"Rule 6: atoms has zero external runtime dependencies.\"\"\"`\n- [`tests/architecture/test_rule_07_sqlite3_confined_to_engine_store.py:1`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/tests/architecture/test_rule_07_sqlite3_confined_to_engine_store.py#L1): `\"\"\"Rule 7: sqlite3 confined to engine and store.\"\"\"`\n- [`tests/architecture/test_rule_08_domain_constants_in_custody_only.py:1`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/tests/architecture/test_rule_08_domain_constants_in_custody_only.py#L1): `\"\"\"Rule 8: signing domain constants live in libs/custody only.\"\"\"`\n- [`tests/architecture/test_rule_09_resolve_local_vertex_ambiguity.py:1`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/tests/architecture/test_rule_09_resolve_local_vertex_ambiguity.py#L1): `\"\"\"Rule 9: every resolve_local_vertex caller handles the ambiguity refusal.\"\"\"`\n- [`tests/architecture/test_rule_10_disclosure_renderers_no_store_io.py:1`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/tests/architecture/test_rule_10_disclosure_renderers_no_store_io.py#L1): `\"\"\"Rule 10: disclosure renderers do no store I/O.\"\"\"`\n- [`tests/architecture/test_rule_11_record_never_imports_surfacing.py:1`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/tests/architecture/test_rule_11_record_never_imports_surfacing.py#L1): `\"\"\"Rule 11: record-layer libs never import surfacing-layer libs.\"\"\"`\n- [`tests/architecture/test_rule_12_render_register_is_offered_width.py:1`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/tests/architecture/test_rule_12_render_register_is_offered_width.py#L1): `\"\"\"Rule 12: the render register IS the offered width.\"\"\"`\n- [`tests/architecture/test_rule_13_production_never_imports_non_production.py:1`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/tests/architecture/test_rule_13_production_never_imports_non_production.py#L1): `\"\"\"Rule 13: production code never imports a non-production root.\"\"\"`\n- [`tests/architecture/test_rule_14_mutation_survivors_shrink_only.py:1`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/tests/architecture/test_rule_14_mutation_survivors_shrink_only.py#L1): `\"\"\"Rule 14: mutation-testing survivors are shrink-only.\"\"\"`\n- [`tests/architecture/test_rule_15_apps_import_only_sdk_and_painted.py:1`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/tests/architecture/test_rule_15_apps_import_only_sdk_and_painted.py#L1): `\"\"\"Rule 15: Apps may import only sdk + painted.\"\"\"`\n- [`tests/architecture/test_rule_16_hot_path_libs_import_footprint.py:1`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/tests/architecture/test_rule_16_hot_path_libs_import_footprint.py#L1): `\"\"\"Rule 16: hot-path libs keep their import footprint (lazy-import ratchet).\"\"\"`\n- [`tests/architecture/test_rule_17_fold_order_prose_is_receipt_order.py:1`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/tests/architecture/test_rule_17_fold_order_prose_is_receipt_order.py#L1): `\"\"\"Rule 17: shipped prose never claims (ts, id) is the fold order.\"\"\"`\n- [`tests/architecture/test_rule_18_arrival_vocabulary_denylist.py:1`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/tests/architecture/test_rule_18_arrival_vocabulary_denylist.py#L1): `\"\"\"Rule 18: the arrival surface never names the superseded vocabulary.\"\"\"`\n\n---\n\n### 5. Rowid-Survival Ratchet from Cut B\n\n- **File**: [`libs/engine/tests/test_arrival_rederivation_rowids.py`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/libs/engine/tests/test_arrival_rederivation_rowids.py)\n- **Test name**: `test_rederivation_reproduces_every_rowid`\n- **Line range**: lines 155–175\n- **Verbatim assertion lines**: [`libs/engine/tests/test_arrival_rederivation_rowids.py:166-174`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/explore-sliceC/libs/engine/tests/test_arrival_rederivation_rowids.py#L166-L174)\n```python\n    assert after[\"facts\"] == before[\"facts\"]\n    assert after[\"ticks\"] == before[\"ticks\"]\n    assert positions(db) == before_positions\n    assert result.facts == len(before[\"facts\"])\n    assert result.ticks == len(before[\"ticks\"])\n    # Not vacuous: rowids are dense from 1, so a renumbering would show.\n    assert [r[0] for r in after[\"facts\"]] == list(\n        range(1, len(after[\"facts\"]) + 1)\n    )\n```\n{\"answer\":\"found\",\"locations\":[{\"file\":\"spec/conformance/vectors/lens/lens-sub-millisecond-timestamp-precision.json\",\"lines\":\"1-25\",\"note\":\"Example vector file for lens conformance testing.\",\"quote\":\"{\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"sub-millisecond-timestamp-precision\\\",\"},{\"file\":\"libs/engine/tests/test_conformance_lens.py\",\"lines\":\"34-36\",\"note\":\"Loader function for lens conformance vectors.\",\"quote\":\"def _load_vectors(vectors_dir: Path) -\\u003e list[Path]:\\n    return sorted(vectors_dir.glob(\\\"*.json\\\"))\"},{\"file\":\"libs/engine/tests/test_conformance_lens.py\",\"lines\":\"74-89\",\"note\":\"Harness executing vectors through lenses via vertex_facts.\",\"quote\":\"@pytest.mark.parametrize(\\n    \\\"vector_path\\\", _load_vectors(LENS_VECTORS_DIR), ids=lambda p: p.stem\\n)\\ndef test_conformance_lens(vector_path: Path, tmp_path: Path) -\\u003e None:\\n    with open(vector_path, encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as f:\\n        vector = json.load(f)\\n\\n    for key in (\\\"name\\\", \\\"description\\\", \\\"input\\\", \\\"expected\\\"):\\n        assert key in vector, f\\\"Vector {vector_path} missing {key!r}\\\"\\n\\n    kind = vector[\\\"input\\\"][\\\"kind\\\"]\\n    parent = _build_combine_vertex(tmp_path, kind, vector[\\\"input\\\"][\\\"members\\\"])\\n\\n    rows = vertex_facts(parent, 0.0, float(\\\"inf\\\"), kind=kind)\\n    assert [r[\\\"id\\\"] for r in rows] == vector[\\\"expected\\\"][\\\"lens_order\\\"]\"},{\"file\":\"libs/engine/tests/test_handle_incremental.py\",\"lines\":\"110-120\",\"note\":\"Test asserting incremental fold equivalence to cold fold at every position.\",\"quote\":\"@settings(max_examples=200, deadline=None)\\n@given(appends=_appends)\\ndef test_incremental_fold_equals_cold_fold_at_every_position(tmp_path_factory, appends):\\n    tmp_path = tmp_path_factory.mktemp(\\\"inc\\\")\\n    vpath, store = _scaffold(tmp_path)\\n    with open_vertex(vpath) as h:\\n        for kind, ts, key, val in appends:\\n            _append(store, kind, ts, **{_KEY_FIELD[kind]: key, \\\"value\\\": val})\\n            batch = h.refresh()\\n            assert batch is not None\\n            assert _items(h.snapshot.fold) == _cold(vpath, h.snapshot.position)\"},{\"file\":\"libs/engine/tests/test_handle_incremental.py\",\"lines\":\"164-173\",\"note\":\"Test verifying replay_mode reports checkpoint-suffix after seeding.\",\"quote\":\"def test_warm_refresh_reports_checkpoint_suffix_after_seeding(tmp_path):\\n    vpath, store = _scaffold(tmp_path)\\n    with open_vertex(vpath) as h:\\n        _append(store, \\\"decision\\\", 100.0, topic=\\\"a\\\")\\n        # the seeding refresh really does replay all of history — it says so\\n        assert h.refresh().replay_mode == \\\"full\\\"\\n        for i in range(5):\\n            _append(store, \\\"decision\\\", 100.0 + i, topic=f\\\"k{i}\\\")\\n            assert h.refresh().replay_mode == \\\"checkpoint-suffix\\\"\"},{\"file\":\"libs/atoms/tests/test_replay.py\",\"lines\":\"119-131\",\"note\":\"Test verifying replay_from produces identical state when replaying a suffix onto a checkpoint.\",\"quote\":\"    def test_suffix_replay_equals_whole_replay_at_every_split(self):\\n        spec = self._spec()\\n        payloads = [\\n            {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"a\\\", \\\"msg\\\": \\\"one\\\"},\\n            {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"b\\\", \\\"msg\\\": \\\"two\\\"},\\n            {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"a\\\", \\\"msg\\\": \\\"three\\\"},\\n            {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"c\\\", \\\"msg\\\": \\\"four\\\"},\\n        ]\\n        whole = spec.replay(payloads)\\n        for cut in range(len(payloads) + 1):\\n            resumed = spec.replay_from(spec.replay(payloads[:cut]), payloads[cut:])\\n            assert resumed == whole, f\\\"split at {cut} diverged\\\"\"},{\"file\":\"tests/architecture/test_rule_17_fold_order_prose_is_receipt_order.py\",\"lines\":\"203-232\",\"note\":\"Rule 17 test verifying shipped prose never claims (ts, id) is fold order.\",\"quote\":\"def test_fold_order_prose_is_receipt_order():\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"No shipped prose claims `(ts, id)` orders the fold.\\n\\n    Fold replay order is receipt order (``rowid``); ``(ts, id)`` is a read lens\\n    (docs/RECEIPT_ORDER_FOLD.md). Comments, docstrings, and spec/docs\\n    Markdown that still describe the old total order are not cosmetic: they are\\n    how the superseded model gets rebuilt in the next reader's head, and they\\n    are invisible to every behavioral test in the repo.\\n\\n    A new hit means one of two things, and the failure message says which to\\n    pick. Relabel the site (say \\\"read lens\\\", say what it projects, or state the\\n    rule it is denying) — that is the fix in almost every case. Or, if the site\\n    is genuinely lens and cannot be phrased without the pattern, add an\\n    allowlist entry with a comment saying WHY it is lens. The allowlist may\\n    only shrink over time; each addition is a small permanent debt.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    found = _found_claims()\\n    unexpected = sorted((p, ln) for p, ln in found if not _allowed(p, ln))\\n\\n    assert not unexpected, (\\n        \\\"Prose claiming `(ts, id)` / ts-ordering as FOLD or REPLAY order \\\"\\n        \\\"(fold order is receipt order — rowid; see \\\"\\n        \\\"docs/RECEIPT_ORDER_FOLD.md):\\\\n\\\"\\n        + \\\"\\\\n\\\".join(f\\\"  {p}: {ln[:120]}\\\" for p, ln in unexpected)\\n        + \\\"\\\\n\\\\nFix by RELABELLING the site as a read lens (preferred), or — if \\\"\\n        \\\"it truly is a lens and cannot avoid the pattern — add a (path, \\\"\\n        \\\"marker) entry to _ALLOWLIST in this file with a comment saying why. \\\"\\n        \\\"The allowlist is shrink-only.\\\"\\n    )\"},{\"file\":\"tests/architecture/test_rule_17_fold_order_prose_is_receipt_order.py\",\"lines\":\"147-179\",\"note\":\"File-selection function in Rule 17 showing filesystem walk and exclusion filter without docs/scratch.\",\"quote\":\"def _scan_targets() -\\u003e list:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Every shipped-prose file this rule judges.\\n\\n    Derived from the filesystem, never hand-enumerated (docs/RATCHETS.md): a\\n    hand-written list is a silent pass for every lib, app, and doc added after\\n    it was written.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    targets: list = []\\n    for production in (\\\"libs\\\", \\\"apps\\\"):\\n        base = REPO_ROOT / production\\n        if not base.is_dir():\\n            continue\\n        for package in sorted(base.iterdir()):\\n            src = package / \\\"src\\\"\\n            if src.is_dir():\\n                targets.extend(src.rglob(\\\"*.py\\\"))\\n    for docs_root in (\\\"spec\\\", \\\"docs\\\"):\\n        base = REPO_ROOT / docs_root\\n        if base.is_dir():\\n            targets.extend(base.rglob(\\\"*.md\\\"))\\n    # Conformance generators: their CASE descriptions are copied verbatim into\\n    # the vectors, which are normative artifacts other implementations read.\\n    generators = REPO_ROOT / \\\"spec\\\" / \\\"conformance\\\"\\n    if generators.is_dir():\\n        targets.extend(sorted(generators.glob(\\\"generate_*.py\\\")))\\n    return [\\n        p\\n        for p in sorted(set(targets))\\n        if \\\"mutants\\\" not in p.parts\\n        and \\\"__pycache__\\\" not in p.parts\\n        and \\\".venv\\\" not in p.parts\\n    ]\"},{\"file\":\"libs/engine/tests/test_arrival_rederivation_rowids.py\",\"lines\":\"155-175\",\"note\":\"The rowid-survival ratchet test and assertions from cut B.\",\"quote\":\"def test_rederivation_reproduces_every_rowid(tmp_path, keys, signer):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"The gate assertion: every ``(rowid, id)`` pair, in both tables, and\\n    every resolved witness position, is IDENTICAL across a re-derivation.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    log, db = build_through_the_write_path(tmp_path, keys, signer)\\n    before = snapshot(db)\\n    before_positions = positions(db)\\n    assert len(before[\\\"facts\\\"]) \\u003e= 8 and len(before[\\\"ticks\\\"]) == 2\\n\\n    result = rederive_projections(log.path)\\n\\n    after = snapshot(db)\\n    assert after[\\\"facts\\\"] == before[\\\"facts\\\"]\\n    assert after[\\\"ticks\\\"] == before[\\\"ticks\\\"]\\n    assert positions(db) == before_positions\\n    assert result.facts == len(before[\\\"facts\\\"])\\n    assert result.ticks == len(before[\\\"ticks\\\"])\\n    # Not vacuous: rowids are dense from 1, so a renumbering would show.\\n    assert [r[0] for r in after[\\\"facts\\\"]] == list(\\n        range(1, len(after[\\\"facts\\\"]) + 1)\\n    )\"}],\"not_covered\":\"None. All questions in the prompt were located and cited in the codebase.\",\"question\":\"Question set regarding test infrastructure for gate and Rule 17: (1) conformance lens vector infrastructure, (2) checkpoint dispatch tests, (3) Rule 17 test and file-selection logic, (4) architecture test suite layout, (5) rowid-survival ratchet from cut B.\",\"search_method\":\"find_by_name, grep_search, view_file, and python ast inspection across tests/ and libs/\",\"toolAction\":\"Completing explorer task\",\"toolSummary\":\"Finish task execution\"}\n","duration_seconds":63.011951,"num_turns":2,"structured_output":{"answer":"found","locations":[{"file":"spec/conformance/vectors/lens/lens-sub-millisecond-timestamp-precision.json","lines":"1-25","note":"Example vector file for lens conformance testing.","quote":"{\n  \"name\": \"sub-millisecond-timestamp-precision\","},{"file":"libs/engine/tests/test_conformance_lens.py","lines":"34-36","note":"Loader function for lens conformance vectors.","quote":"def _load_vectors(vectors_dir: Path) -\u003e list[Path]:\n    return sorted(vectors_dir.glob(\"*.json\"))"},{"file":"libs/engine/tests/test_conformance_lens.py","lines":"74-89","note":"Harness executing vectors through lenses via vertex_facts.","quote":"@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n    \"vector_path\", _load_vectors(LENS_VECTORS_DIR), ids=lambda p: p.stem\n)\ndef test_conformance_lens(vector_path: Path, tmp_path: Path) -\u003e None:\n    with open(vector_path, encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        vector = json.load(f)\n\n    for key in (\"name\", \"description\", \"input\", \"expected\"):\n        assert key in vector, f\"Vector {vector_path} missing {key!r}\"\n\n    kind = vector[\"input\"][\"kind\"]\n    parent = _build_combine_vertex(tmp_path, kind, vector[\"input\"][\"members\"])\n\n    rows = vertex_facts(parent, 0.0, float(\"inf\"), kind=kind)\n    assert [r[\"id\"] for r in rows] == vector[\"expected\"][\"lens_order\"]"},{"file":"libs/engine/tests/test_handle_incremental.py","lines":"110-120","note":"Test asserting incremental fold equivalence to cold fold at every position.","quote":"@settings(max_examples=200, deadline=None)\n@given(appends=_appends)\ndef test_incremental_fold_equals_cold_fold_at_every_position(tmp_path_factory, appends):\n    tmp_path = tmp_path_factory.mktemp(\"inc\")\n    vpath, store = _scaffold(tmp_path)\n    with open_vertex(vpath) as h:\n        for kind, ts, key, val in appends:\n            _append(store, kind, ts, **{_KEY_FIELD[kind]: key, \"value\": val})\n            batch = h.refresh()\n            assert batch is not None\n            assert _items(h.snapshot.fold) == _cold(vpath, h.snapshot.position)"},{"file":"libs/engine/tests/test_handle_incremental.py","lines":"164-173","note":"Test verifying replay_mode reports checkpoint-suffix after seeding.","quote":"def test_warm_refresh_reports_checkpoint_suffix_after_seeding(tmp_path):\n    vpath, store = _scaffold(tmp_path)\n    with open_vertex(vpath) as h:\n        _append(store, \"decision\", 100.0, topic=\"a\")\n        # the seeding refresh really does replay all of history — it says so\n        assert h.refresh().replay_mode == \"full\"\n        for i in range(5):\n            _append(store, \"decision\", 100.0 + i, topic=f\"k{i}\")\n            assert h.refresh().replay_mode == \"checkpoint-suffix\""},{"file":"libs/atoms/tests/test_replay.py","lines":"119-131","note":"Test verifying replay_from produces identical state when replaying a suffix onto a checkpoint.","quote":"    def test_suffix_replay_equals_whole_replay_at_every_split(self):\n        spec = self._spec()\n        payloads = [\n            {\"topic\": \"a\", \"msg\": \"one\"},\n            {\"topic\": \"b\", \"msg\": \"two\"},\n            {\"topic\": \"a\", \"msg\": \"three\"},\n            {\"topic\": \"c\", \"msg\": \"four\"},\n        ]\n        whole = spec.replay(payloads)\n        for cut in range(len(payloads) + 1):\n            resumed = spec.replay_from(spec.replay(payloads[:cut]), payloads[cut:])\n            assert resumed == whole, f\"split at {cut} diverged\""},{"file":"tests/architecture/test_rule_17_fold_order_prose_is_receipt_order.py","lines":"203-232","note":"Rule 17 test verifying shipped prose never claims (ts, id) is fold order.","quote":"def test_fold_order_prose_is_receipt_order():\n    \"\"\"No shipped prose claims `(ts, id)` orders the fold.\n\n    Fold replay order is receipt order (``rowid``); ``(ts, id)`` is a read lens\n    (docs/RECEIPT_ORDER_FOLD.md). Comments, docstrings, and spec/docs\n    Markdown that still describe the old total order are not cosmetic: they are\n    how the superseded model gets rebuilt in the next reader's head, and they\n    are invisible to every behavioral test in the repo.\n\n    A new hit means one of two things, and the failure message says which to\n    pick. Relabel the site (say \"read lens\", say what it projects, or state the\n    rule it is denying) — that is the fix in almost every case. Or, if the site\n    is genuinely lens and cannot be phrased without the pattern, add an\n    allowlist entry with a comment saying WHY it is lens. The allowlist may\n    only shrink over time; each addition is a small permanent debt.\n    \"\"\"\n    found = _found_claims()\n    unexpected = sorted((p, ln) for p, ln in found if not _allowed(p, ln))\n\n    assert not unexpected, (\n        \"Prose claiming `(ts, id)` / ts-ordering as FOLD or REPLAY order \"\n        \"(fold order is receipt order — rowid; see \"\n        \"docs/RECEIPT_ORDER_FOLD.md):\\n\"\n        + \"\\n\".join(f\"  {p}: {ln[:120]}\" for p, ln in unexpected)\n        + \"\\n\\nFix by RELABELLING the site as a read lens (preferred), or — if \"\n        \"it truly is a lens and cannot avoid the pattern — add a (path, \"\n        \"marker) entry to _ALLOWLIST in this file with a comment saying why. \"\n        \"The allowlist is shrink-only.\"\n    )"},{"file":"tests/architecture/test_rule_17_fold_order_prose_is_receipt_order.py","lines":"147-179","note":"File-selection function in Rule 17 showing filesystem walk and exclusion filter without docs/scratch.","quote":"def _scan_targets() -\u003e list:\n    \"\"\"Every shipped-prose file this rule judges.\n\n    Derived from the filesystem, never hand-enumerated (docs/RATCHETS.md): a\n    hand-written list is a silent pass for every lib, app, and doc added after\n    it was written.\n    \"\"\"\n    targets: list = []\n    for production in (\"libs\", \"apps\"):\n        base = REPO_ROOT / production\n        if not base.is_dir():\n            continue\n        for package in sorted(base.iterdir()):\n            src = package / \"src\"\n            if src.is_dir():\n                targets.extend(src.rglob(\"*.py\"))\n    for docs_root in (\"spec\", \"docs\"):\n        base = REPO_ROOT / docs_root\n        if base.is_dir():\n            targets.extend(base.rglob(\"*.md\"))\n    # Conformance generators: their CASE descriptions are copied verbatim into\n    # the vectors, which are normative artifacts other implementations read.\n    generators = REPO_ROOT / \"spec\" / \"conformance\"\n    if generators.is_dir():\n        targets.extend(sorted(generators.glob(\"generate_*.py\")))\n    return [\n        p\n        for p in sorted(set(targets))\n        if \"mutants\" not in p.parts\n        and \"__pycache__\" not in p.parts\n        and \".venv\" not in p.parts\n    ]"},{"file":"libs/engine/tests/test_arrival_rederivation_rowids.py","lines":"155-175","note":"The rowid-survival ratchet test and assertions from cut B.","quote":"def test_rederivation_reproduces_every_rowid(tmp_path, keys, signer):\n    \"\"\"The gate assertion: every ``(rowid, id)`` pair, in both tables, and\n    every resolved witness position, is IDENTICAL across a re-derivation.\"\"\"\n    log, db = build_through_the_write_path(tmp_path, keys, signer)\n    before = snapshot(db)\n    before_positions = positions(db)\n    assert len(before[\"facts\"]) \u003e= 8 and len(before[\"ticks\"]) == 2\n\n    result = rederive_projections(log.path)\n\n    after = snapshot(db)\n    assert after[\"facts\"] == before[\"facts\"]\n    assert after[\"ticks\"] == before[\"ticks\"]\n    assert positions(db) == before_positions\n    assert result.facts == len(before[\"facts\"])\n    assert result.ticks == len(before[\"ticks\"])\n    # Not vacuous: rowids are dense from 1, so a renumbering would show.\n    assert [r[0] for r in after[\"facts\"]] == list(\n        range(1, len(after[\"facts\"]) + 1)\n    )"}],"not_covered":"None. All questions in the prompt were located and cited in the codebase.","question":"Question set regarding test infrastructure for gate and Rule 17: (1) conformance lens vector infrastructure, (2) checkpoint dispatch tests, (3) Rule 17 test and file-selection logic, (4) architecture test suite layout, (5) rowid-survival ratchet from cut B.","search_method":"find_by_name, grep_search, view_file, and python ast inspection across tests/ and libs/"},"json_schema":{"$comment":"Explorer output contract. Shapes recon as LOCATION claims the arbiter can grep, not verdict claims the arbiter would have to trust. Pass with --output-format=json --json-schema=\u003cthis file\u003e; read the result at .structured_output.","type":"object","properties":{"question":{"typ