docs/scratch/arrival-sliceC/explorers/e5-fold-fork-keeps.json:1:{"conversation_id":"4e238508-6dc6-4985-abcd-1d84a1afa31d","status":"SUCCESS","response":"{\"answer\":\"found\",\"locations\":[{\"file\":\"libs/engine/src/engine/vertex_reader.py\",\"lines\":\"347-445\",\"note\":\"Definition of _combined_read including the single_store sort branch (lines 403-406) and docstring/context around line 390.\",\"quote\":\"def _combined_read(\\n    ast: Any, vertex_path: Path, specs: dict, *, observer: str | None = None,\\n    return_payloads: bool = False,\\n    until_ts: float | None = None,\\n) -\\u003e \\\"dict[str, dict[str, Any]] | tuple[dict[str, dict[str, Any]], dict[str, list[dict]]]\\\":\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Fold state across multiple stores (combinatorial vertex_read).\\n\\n    Fetches all facts in a single SQL query across attached stores,\\n    then groups by kind and replays through specs. Single query avoids\\n    the SQLite cold-start penalty (~10ms) that would hit the first of\\n    N per-kind queries.\\n\\n    When ``return_payloads=True``, returns ``(raw_state, kind_payloads)``\\n    so callers can use the per-kind payload lists for retain_facts /\\n    source_facts population without re-querying the stores.\\n\\n    ``until_ts`` (0.8.0 fold-state-``as_of``, A9) caps every member's facts\\n    to ``ts \\u003c= until_ts`` — the event-time projection over an aggregate.\\n    Membership itself stays CURRENT file state regardless (aggregation\\n    internal tables are not yet built, the shipped \\\"aggregate-head\\\" honesty\\n    marker) — only the facts axis is cut by the cursor.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    store_paths = _resolve_stores(ast, vertex_path)\\n    if not store_paths:\\n        empty_raw = {kind: spec.initial_state() for kind, spec in specs.items()}\\n        if return_payloads:\\n            return empty_raw, {k: [] for k in specs}\\n        return empty_raw\\n\\n    conn, aliases = _open_combined(store_paths)\\n    try:\\n        # Single query for all facts, fold-replay-ordered.\\n        #\\n        # Single store: receipt order (rowid ASC) — the ratified fold axis,\\n        # matching StoreReader.facts_by_kind.\\n        #\\n        # Multiple stores: rowid is PER-STORE, so a combined view has no\\n        # receipt axis to fold on. These reads fall back to the explicit\\n        # (ts, id) READ LENS ordering — same rule as facts_in_range below.\\n        # A combined fold is therefore a lens projection, not a receipt\\n        # replay, and may disagree with a single-store fold of the same\\n        # facts. Named interim state pending the multi-store receipt-order\\n        # ruling.\\n        single_store = len(aliases) == 1\\n        ts_clause = \\\" WHERE ts \\u003c= ?\\\" if until_ts is not None else \\\"\\\"\\n        selects = [\\n            f\\\"SELECT id, kind, ts, observer, origin, payload, rowid \\\"\\n            f\\\"FROM {'[' + a + '].' if a != 'main' else ''}facts{ts_clause}\\\"\\n            for a in aliases\\n        ]\\n        sql = \\\" UNION ALL \\\".join(selects)\\n        params = (until_ts,) * len(aliases) if until_ts is not None else ()\\n\\n        rows = conn.execute(sql, params).fetchall()\\n        # Sort in Python — avoids a SQLite index scan for the ORDER BY,\\n        # which causes random I/O (~14ms vs ~1ms for unsorted read).\\n        if single_store:\\n            rows.sort(key=lambda r: r[6])\\n        else:\\n            rows.sort(key=lambda r: (r[2], r[0]))\\n\\n        # Build kind → spec lookup, including sub-kind (dot-prefix) routing.\\n        # \\\"thread.foo\\\" → \\\"thread\\\" if \\\"thread\\\" is a spec kind.\\n        spec_kinds = set(specs)\\n        kind_payloads: dict[str, list] = {k: [] for k in specs}\\n\\n        for r in rows:\\n            kind = r[1]\\n            if observer and not observer_matches(r[3], observer):\\n                continue\\n            # Exact match\\n            if kind in spec_kinds:\\n                target = kind\\n            else:\\n                # Sub-kind: \\\"foo.bar\\\" → check \\\"foo\\\"\\n                dot = kind.find(\\\".\\\")\\n                if dot \\u003c 0:\\n                    continue\\n                prefix = kind[:dot]\\n                if prefix not in spec_kinds:\\n                    continue\\n                target = prefix\\n            p = json.loads(r[5])\\n            p[\\\"_id\\\"] = r[0]\\n            p[\\\"_ts\\\"] = r[2]\\n            p[\\\"_observer\\\"] = r[3]\\n            p[\\\"_origin\\\"] = r[4] or \\\"\\\"\\n            kind_payloads[target].append(p)\\n\\n        raw = {\\n            kind: spec.replay(kind_payloads[kind])\\n            for kind, spec in specs.items()\\n        }\\n        if return_payloads:\\n            return raw, kind_payloads\\n        return raw\\n    finally:\\n        conn.close()\"},{\"file\":\"libs/sdk/src/sdk/read.py\",\"lines\":\"106-241\",\"note\":\"read_summary handles combined read across stores when target is an aggregate vertex.\",\"quote\":\"    if info.target_type == \\\"vertex\\\":\\n        decl_ast, decl_status = load_declaration_status(target_path)\\n        is_aggregate = decl_ast is not None and (\\n            decl_ast.combine is not None or decl_ast.discover is not None\\n        )\\n\\n        if not is_aggregate and (info.canonical_path is None or not info.canonical_path.exists()):\\n            return ReadSummary(\\n                target_type=\\\"vertex\\\",\\n                target_path=str(target_path),\\n                canonical_mode=info.canonical_mode or \\\"unknown\\\",\\n                canonical_path=str(info.canonical_path) if info.canonical_path else None,\\n                index_path=str(info.index_path) if info.index_path else None,\\n                declaration_status=decl_status or \\\"unknown\\\",\\n                fact_total=0,\\n                tick_total=0,\\n                latest_ts=None,\\n                kinds={},\\n                unfolded_kinds=[],\\n                agreement=True,\\n                signed_count=0,\\n                unsigned_count=0,\\n            )\\n\\n        if is_aggregate:\\n            raw_sum = vertex_summary(target_path, include_internal=include_internal)\\n            fact_total = raw_sum.get(\\\"facts\\\", {}).get(\\\"total\\\", 0)\\n            tick_total = raw_sum.get(\\\"ticks\\\", {}).get(\\\"total\\\", 0)\\n            kinds_raw = raw_sum.get(\\\"facts\\\", {}).get(\\\"kinds\\\", {})\\n            kinds = {\\n                k: {\\n                    \\\"count\\\": v.get(\\\"count\\\", 0),\\n                    \\\"earliest\\\": v.get(\\\"earliest\\\"),\\n                    \\\"latest\\\": v.get(\\\"latest\\\"),\\n                }\\n                for k, v in kinds_raw.items()\\n            }\\n            return ReadSummary(\\n                target_type=\\\"vertex\\\",\\n                target_path=str(target_path),\\n                canonical_mode=info.canonical_mode or \\\"aggregate\\\",\\n                canonical_path=str(info.canonical_path) if info.canonical_path else None,\\n                index_path=str(info.index_path) if info.index_path else None,\\n                declaration_status=decl_status or \\\"aggregate-head\\\",\\n                fact_total=fact_total,\\n                tick_total=tick_total,\\n                latest_ts=None,\\n                kinds=kinds,\\n                unfolded_kinds=[],\\n                agreement=True,\\n                signed_count=0,\\n                unsigned_count=fact_total,\\n            )\"},{\"file\":\"libs/sdk/src/sdk/read.py\",\"lines\":\"244-384\",\"note\":\"read_facts handles combined read across stores when target is an aggregate vertex.\",\"quote\":\"    if info.target_type == \\\"vertex\\\":\\n        decl_ast, _ = load_declaration_status(target_path)\\n        is_aggregate = decl_ast is not None and (\\n            decl_ast.combine is not None or decl_ast.discover is not None\\n        )\\n\\n        if is_aggregate:\\n            # Multi-store aggregate vertex\\n            all_facts = vertex_facts(\\n                target_path,\\n                since_ts=0.0,\\n                until_ts=float(\\\"inf\\\"),\\n                kind=kind,\\n                observer=observer,\\n                include_internal=include_internal,\\n            )\\n            if order == \\\"newest\\\":\\n                all_facts = list(reversed(all_facts))\\n\\n            capped = all_facts[:limit]\\n            truncated = len(all_facts) \\u003e len(capped)\\n            return FactPageResult(\\n                items=capped,\\n                next_cursor=None,\\n                prev_cursor=None,\\n                truncated=truncated,\\n                order=order,\\n            )\"},{\"file\":\"libs/sdk/src/sdk/read.py\",\"lines\":\"430-481\",\"note\":\"read_state performs combined state fold via vertex_read.\",\"quote\":\"    target_path = Path(target).resolve()\\n    decl_ast, decl_status = load_declaration_status(target_path)\\n    vertex_path = target_path\\n\\n    if info.canonical_path is None or not info.canonical_path.exists():\\n        return FoldStateResult(\\n            vertex_name=decl_ast.name if decl_ast else vertex_path.stem,\\n            target_path=str(vertex_path),\\n            declaration_status=decl_status or \\\"unknown\\\",\\n            generation={},\\n            sections={},\\n        )\\n\\n    state_dict = vertex_read(vertex_path, observer=observer)\"},{\"file\":\"libs/sdk/src/sdk/read.py\",\"lines\":\"484-521\",\"note\":\"read_ticks handles combined ticks across stores for aggregate vertices.\",\"quote\":\"    if info.target_type == \\\"vertex\\\":\\n        decl_ast, _ = load_declaration_status(target_path)\\n        is_aggregate = decl_ast is not None and (\\n            decl_ast.combine is not None or decl_ast.discover is not None\\n        )\\n        if is_aggregate:\\n            ticks = vertex_ticks(target_path, 0.0, float(\\\"inf\\\"), name=name)\\n            return [_tick_as_dict(t) for t in ticks]\"},{\"file\":\"libs/sdk/src/sdk/read.py\",\"lines\":\"523-557\",\"note\":\"read_fact_by_id handles fact lookup on aggregate vertices.\",\"quote\":\"    if info.target_type == \\\"vertex\\\":\\n        decl_ast, _ = load_declaration_status(target_path)\\n        is_aggregate = decl_ast is not None and (\\n            decl_ast.combine is not None or decl_ast.discover is not None\\n        )\\n        if is_aggregate:\\n            return vertex_fact_by_id(target_path, fact_id)\"},{\"file\":\"libs/sdk/src/sdk/read.py\",\"lines\":\"560-662\",\"note\":\"search_facts handles combined full-text search across stores for aggregate vertices.\",\"quote\":\"    if info.target_type == \\\"vertex\\\":\\n        try:\\n            raw_matches = vertex_search(target_path, query, kind=kind, limit=limit)\"},{\"file\":\"libs/sdk/src/sdk/read.py\",\"lines\":\"664-727\",\"note\":\"resolve_entity branches on aggregate single-store vs multi-store combined read.\",\"quote\":\"        if is_aggregate:\\n            # Entity resolution must agree with the fold, so it mirrors\\n            # _combined_read's member-count branch via the same helper.\\n            #\\n            # ONE member: that member's rowid IS the aggregate's receipt\\n            # axis, so the fold replays in receipt order and resolution\\n            # must too — a backdated re-assertion wins the fold, and the\\n            # lens walk below would hand back the row it superseded.\\n            #\\n            # TWO OR MORE: rowid is per-store, so no shared receipt axis\\n            # exists. The combined read falls back to the event-time lens\\n            # and every other combined surface reads through that same\\n            # lens, so the lens walk below is the coherent answer.\\n            store_paths = _resolve_stores(decl_ast, target_path)\\n            if len(store_paths) == 1 and store_paths[0].exists():\\n                member_reader = StoreReader(store_paths[0])\\n                try:\\n                    return member_reader.resolve_entity_id(kind, key, value)\\n                finally:\\n                    member_reader.close()\\n\\n            all_facts = vertex_facts(target_path, since_ts=0.0, until_ts=float(\\\"inf\\\"), kind=kind)\\n            for f in reversed(all_facts):\\n                p = f.get(\\\"payload\\\", {})\\n                if str(p.get(key)) == str(value):\\n                    return f.get(\\\"id\\\")\\n            return None\"},{\"file\":\"libs/sdk/src/sdk/read.py\",\"lines\":\"729-899\",\"note\":\"read_timeline handles interleaved timeline read across aggregate stores.\",\"quote\":\"    if info.target_type == \\\"vertex\\\":\\n        decl_ast, _ = load_declaration_status(target_path)\\n        is_aggregate = decl_ast is not None and (\\n            decl_ast.combine is not None or decl_ast.discover is not None\\n        )\\n\\n        if is_aggregate or (info.canonical_path is not None and info.canonical_path.exists()):\\n            raw_facts = vertex_facts(target_path, since_ts=since, until_ts=until)\\n            for f in raw_facts:\\n                f_ts = (\\n                    f[\\\"ts\\\"].timestamp()\\n                    if hasattr(f.get(\\\"ts\\\"), \\\"timestamp\\\")\\n                    else float(f.get(\\\"ts\\\", 0.0))\\n                )\\n                events.append(\\n                    TimelineEvent(\\n                        event_type=\\\"fact\\\",\\n                        id=f.get(\\\"id\\\", \\\"\\\"),\\n                        kind_or_name=f.get(\\\"kind\\\", \\\"\\\"),\\n                        ts=f_ts,\\n                        observer=f.get(\\\"observer\\\", \\\"\\\"),\\n                        origin=f.get(\\\"origin\\\", \\\"\\\"),\\n                        payload=dict(f.get(\\\"payload\\\", {})),\\n                    )\\n                )\\n\\n            raw_ticks = vertex_ticks(target_path, since, until)\"},{\"file\":\"libs/atoms/src/atoms/spec.py\",\"lines\":\"128-148\",\"note\":\"Spec.replay_from definition for suffix replay.\",\"quote\":\"    def replay_from(\\n        self, state: dict[str, Any], payloads: Iterable[dict[str, Any]]\\n    ) -\\u003e dict[str, Any]:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Suffix replay: continue folding from an existing ``state``.\\n\\n        Copies ``state`` ONCE (deep, as ``apply()`` does) and then mutates that\\n        copy across every payload — the per-payload cost of ``replay()`` with\\n        the input-purity of ``apply()``. Valid only when the fold replay order\\n        is append order, so that a suffix of the receipt stream can be applied\\n        to the state folded from its prefix.\\n\\n        The single deep copy is load-bearing for callers that keep a long-lived\\n        checkpoint (``engine.handle``): the input ``state`` is never mutated, so\\n        it may stay shared with an already-published snapshot.\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        fns = self._cached_fold_fns\\n        new = copy.deepcopy(state)\\n        for payload in payloads:\\n            for fn in fns:\\n                fn(new, payload)\\n        return new\"},{\"file\":\"libs/engine/src/engine/handle.py\",\"lines\":\"752-1340\",\"note\":\"VertexHandle checkpoint machinery and state reconstruction methods.\",\"quote\":\"class VertexHandle:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"A held, recompilable vertex session whose source of truth stays SQLite.\\n\\n    Serializes ``refresh()`` and ``receive()`` under one lock and permits one\\n    active change iterator. Snapshot values are immutable and may be handed to a\\n    painter. Multiple independent subscriptions use independent handles.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\"},{\"file\":\"benchmarks/characterize.py\",\"lines\":\"206-224\",\"note\":\"Benchmark arm probe_store touching ingest/append and store scan.\",\"quote\":\"def probe_store(depth: int) -\\u003e list[Sample]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Raw SqliteStore append and full-scan cost at `depth` existing rows.\\\"\\\"\\\"\"},{\"file\":\"benchmarks/characterize.py\",\"lines\":\"242-320\",\"note\":\"Benchmark arm probe_vertex_layers touching fold, receive (ingest), and cold open.\",\"quote\":\"def probe_vertex_layers(depth: int, include_sdk: bool) -\\u003e list[Sample]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Engine and (when present) sdk probes against one vertex filled to `depth`.\"}],\"not_covered\":\"None. Looked in all requested locations across engine, sdk, atoms, and benchmarks.\",\"question\":\"Combined-read fold fork, sdk read path, combined-read callers, and KEEP-fence locations in explore/arrival-sliceC.\",\"search_method\":\"git branch verification, find_by_name, grep_search, view_file\",\"toolAction\":\"Finish exploration task\",\"toolSummary\":\"Complete exploration task\"}\n","duration_seconds":54.544373,"num_turns":1,"structured_output":{"answer":"found","locations":[{"file":"libs/engine/src/engine/vertex_reader.py","lines":"347-445","note":"Definition of _combined_read including the single_store sort branch (lines 403-406) and docstring/context around line 390.","quote":"def _combined_read(\n    ast: Any, vertex_path: Path, specs: dict, *, observer: str | None = None,\n    return_payloads: bool = False,\n    until_ts: float | None = None,\n) -\u003e \"dict[str, dict[str, Any]] | tuple[dict[str, dict[str, Any]], dict[str, list[dict]]]\":\n    \"\"\"Fold state across multiple stores (combinatorial vertex_read).\n\n    Fetches all facts in a single SQL query across attached stores,\n    then groups by kind and replays through specs. Single query avoids\n    the SQLite cold-start penalty (~10ms) that would hit the first of\n    N per-kind queries.\n\n    When ``return_payloads=True``, returns ``(raw_state, kind_payloads)``\n    so callers can use the per-kind payload lists for retain_facts /\n    source_facts population without re-querying the stores.\n\n    ``until_ts`` (0.8.0 fold-state-``as_of``, A9) caps every member's facts\n    to ``ts \u003c= until_ts`` — the event-time projection over an aggregate.\n    Membership itself stays CURRENT file state regardless (aggregation\n    internal tables are not yet built, the shipped \"aggregate-head\" honesty\n    marker) — only the facts axis is cut by the cursor.\n    \"\"\"\n    store_paths = _resolve_stores(ast, vertex_path)\n    if not store_paths:\n        empty_raw = {kind: spec.initial_state() for kind, spec in specs.items()}\n        if return_payloads:\n            return empty_raw, {k: [] for k in specs}\n        return empty_raw\n\n    conn, aliases = _open_combined(store_paths)\n    try:\n        # Single query for all facts, fold-replay-ordered.\n        #\n        # Single store: receipt order (rowid ASC) — the ratified fold axis,\n        # matching StoreReader.facts_by_kind.\n        #\n        # Multiple stores: rowid is PER-STORE, so a combined view has no\n        # receipt axis to fold on. These reads fall back to the explicit\n        # (ts, id) READ LENS ordering — same rule as facts_in_range below.\n        # A combined fold is therefore a lens projection, not a receipt\n        # replay, and may disagree with a single-store fold of the same\n        # facts. Named interim state pending the multi-store receipt-order\n        # ruling.\n        single_store = len(aliases) == 1\n        ts_clause = \" WHERE ts \u003c= ?\" if until_ts is not None else \"\"\n        selects = [\n            f\"SELECT id, kind, ts, observer, origin, payload, rowid \"\n            f\"FROM {'[' + a + '].' if a != 'main' else ''}facts{ts_clause}\"\n            for a in aliases\n        ]\n        sql = \" UNION ALL \".join(selects)\n        params = (until_ts,) * len(aliases) if until_ts is not None else ()\n\n        rows = conn.execute(sql, params).fetchall()\n        # Sort in Python — avoids a SQLite index scan for the ORDER BY,\n        # which causes random I/O (~14ms vs ~1ms for unsorted read).\n        if single_store:\n            rows.sort(key=lambda r: r[6])\n        else:\n            rows.sort(key=lambda r: (r[2], r[0]))\n\n        # Build kind → spec lookup, including sub-kind (dot-prefix) routing.\n        # \"thread.foo\" → \"thread\" if \"thread\" is a spec kind.\n        spec_kinds = set(specs)\n        kind_payloads: dict[str, list] = {k: [] for k in specs}\n\n        for r in rows:\n            kind = r[1]\n            if observer and not observer_matches(r[3], observer):\n                continue\n            # Exact match\n            if kind in spec_kinds:\n                target = kind\n            else:\n                # Sub-kind: \"foo.bar\" → check \"foo\"\n                dot = kind.find(\".\")\n                if dot \u003c 0:\n                    continue\n                prefix = kind[:dot]\n                if prefix not in spec_kinds:\n                    continue\n                target = prefix\n            p = json.loads(r[5])\n            p[\"_id\"] = r[0]\n            p[\"_ts\"] = r[2]\n            p[\"_observer\"] = r[3]\n            p[\"_origin\"] = r[4] or \"\"\n            kind_payloads[target].append(p)\n\n        raw = {\n            kind: spec.replay(kind_payloads[kind])\n            for kind, spec in specs.items()\n        }\n        if return_payloads:\n            return raw, kind_payloads\n        return raw\n    finally:\n        conn.close()"},{"file":"libs/sdk/src/sdk/read.py","lines":"106-241","note":"read_summary handles combined read across stores when target is an aggregate vertex.","quote":"    if info.target_type == \"vertex\":\n        decl_ast, decl_status = load_declaration_status(target_path)\n        is_aggregate = decl_ast is not None and (\n            decl_ast.combine is not None or decl_ast.discover is not None\n        )\n\n        if not is_aggregate and (info.canonical_path is None or not info.canonical_path.exists()):\n            return ReadSummary(\n                target_type=\"vertex\",\n                target_path=str(target_path),\n                canonical_mode=info.canonical_mode or \"unknown\",\n                canonical_path=str(info.canonical_path) if info.canonical_path else None,\n                index_path=str(info.index_path) if info.index_path else None,\n                declaration_status=decl_status or \"unknown\",\n                fact_total=0,\n                tick_total=0,\n                latest_ts=None,\n                kinds={},\n                unfolded_kinds=[],\n                agreement=True,\n                signed_count=0,\n                unsigned_count=0,\n            )\n\n        if is_aggregate:\n            raw_sum = vertex_summary(target_path, include_internal=include_internal)\n            fact_total = raw_sum.get(\"facts\", {}).get(\"total\", 0)\n            tick_total = raw_sum.get(\"ticks\", {}).get(\"total\", 0)\n            kinds_raw = raw_sum.get(\"facts\", {}).get(\"kinds\", {})\n            kinds = {\n                k: {\n                    \"count\": v.get(\"count\", 0),\n                    \"earliest\": v.get(\"earliest\"),\n                    \"latest\": v.get(\"latest\"),\n                }\n                for k, v in kinds_raw.items()\n            }\n            return ReadSummary(\n                target_type=\"vertex\",\n                target_path=str(target_path),\n                canonical_mode=info.canonical_mode or \"aggregate\",\n                canonical_path=str(info.canonical_path) if info.canonical_path else None,\n                index_path=str(info.index_path) if info.index_path else None,\n                declaration_status=decl_status or \"aggregate-head\",\n                fact_total=fact_total,\n                tick_total=tick_total,\n                latest_ts=None,\n                kinds=kinds,\n                unfolded_kinds=[],\n                agreement=True,\n                signed_count=0,\n                unsigned_count=fact_total,\n            )"},{"file":"libs/sdk/src/sdk/read.py","lines":"244-384","note":"read_facts handles combined read across stores when target is an aggregate vertex.","quote":"    if info.target_type == \"vertex\":\n        decl_ast, _ = load_declaration_status(target_path)\n        is_aggregate = decl_ast is not None and (\n            decl_ast.combine is not None or decl_ast.discover is not None\n        )\n\n        if is_aggregate:\n            # Multi-store aggregate vertex\n            all_facts = vertex_facts(\n                target_path,\n                since_ts=0.0,\n                until_ts=float(\"inf\"),\n                kind=kind,\n                observer=observer,\n                include_internal=include_internal,\n            )\n            if order == \"newest\":\n                all_facts = list(reversed(all_facts))\n\n            capped = all_facts[:limit]\n            truncated = len(all_facts) \u003e len(capped)\n            return FactPageResult(\n                items=capped,\n                next_cursor=None,\n                prev_cursor=None,\n                truncated=truncated,\n                order=order,\n            )"},{"file":"libs/sdk/src/sdk/read.py","lines":"430-481","note":"read_state performs combined state fold via vertex_read.","quote":"    target_path = Path(target).resolve()\n    decl_ast, decl_status = load_declaration_status(target_path)\n    vertex_path = target_path\n\n    if info.canonical_path is None or not info.canonical_path.exists():\n        return FoldStateResult(\n            vertex_name=decl_ast.name if decl_ast else vertex_path.stem,\n            target_path=str(vertex_path),\n            declaration_status=decl_status or \"unknown\",\n            generation={},\n            sections={},\n        )\n\n    state_dict = vertex_read(vertex_path, observer=observer)"},{"file":"libs/sdk/src/sdk/read.py","lines":"484-521","note":"read_ticks handles combined ticks across stores for aggregate vertices.","quote":"    if info.target_type == \"vertex\":\n        decl_ast, _ = load_declaration_status(target_path)\n        is_aggregate = decl_ast is not None and (\n            decl_ast.combine is not None or decl_ast.discover is not None\n        )\n        if is_aggregate:\n            ticks = vertex_ticks(target_path, 0.0, float(\"inf\"), name=name)\n            return [_tick_as_dict(t) for t in ticks]"},{"file":"libs/sdk/src/sdk/read.py","lines":"523-557","note":"read_fact_by_id handles fact lookup on aggregate vertices.","quote":"    if info.target_type == \"vertex\":\n        decl_ast, _ = load_declaration_status(target_path)\n        is_aggregate = decl_ast is not None and (\n            decl_ast.combine is not None or decl_ast.discover is not None\n        )\n        if is_aggregate:\n            return vertex_fact_by_id(target_path, fact_id)"},{"file":"libs/sdk/src/sdk/read.py","lines":"560-662","note":"search_facts handles combined full-text search across stores for aggregate vertices.","quote":"    if info.target_type == \"vertex\":\n        try:\n            raw_matches = vertex_search(target_path, query, kind=kind, limit=limit)"},{"file":"libs/sdk/src/sdk/read.py","lines":"664-727","note":"resolve_entity branches on aggregate single-store vs multi-store combined read.","quote":"        if is_aggregate:\n            # Entity resolution must agree with the fold, so it mirrors\n            # _combined_read's member-count branch via the same helper.\n            #\n            # ONE member: that member's rowid IS the aggregate's receipt\n            # axis, so the fold replays in receipt order and resolution\n            # must too — a backdated re-assertion wins the fold, and the\n            # lens walk below would hand back the row it superseded.\n            #\n            # TWO OR MORE: rowid is per-store, so no shared receipt axis\n            # exists. The combined read falls back to the event-time lens\n            # and every other combined surface reads through that same\n            # lens, so the lens walk below is the coherent answer.\n            store_paths = _resolve_stores(decl_ast, target_path)\n            if len(store_paths) == 1 and store_paths[0].exists():\n                member_reader = StoreReader(store_paths[0])\n                try:\n                    return member_reader.resolve_entity_id(kind, key, value)\n                finally:\n                    member_reader.close()\n\n            all_facts = vertex_facts(target_path, since_ts=0.0, until_ts=float(\"inf\"), kind=kind)\n            for f in reversed(all_facts):\n                p = f.get(\"payload\", {})\n                if str(p.get(key)) == str(value):\n                    return f.get(\"id\")\n            return None"},{"file":"libs/sdk/src/sdk/read.py","lines":"729-899","note":"read_timeline handles interleaved timeline read across aggregate stores.","quote":"    if info.target_type == \"vertex\":\n        decl_ast, _ = load_declaration_status(target_path)\n        is_aggregate = decl_ast is not None and (\n            decl_ast.combine is not None or decl_ast.discover is not None\n        )\n\n        if is_aggregate or (info.canonical_path is not None and info.canonical_path.exists()):\n            raw_facts = vertex_facts(target_path, since_ts=since, until_ts=until)\n            for f in raw_facts:\n                f_ts = (\n                    f[\"ts\"].timestamp()\n                    if hasattr(f.get(\"ts\"), \"timestamp\")\n                    else float(f.get(\"ts\", 0.0))\n                )\n                events.append(\n                    TimelineEvent(\n                        event_type=\"fact\",\n                        id=f.get(\"id\", \"\"),\n                        kind_or_name=f.get(\"kind\", \"\"),\n                        ts=f_ts,\n                        observer=f.get(\"observer\", \"\"),\n                        origin=f.get(\"origin\", \"\"),\n                        payload=dict(f.get(\"payload\", {})),\n                    )\n                )\n\n            raw_ticks = vertex_ticks(target_path, since, until)"},{"file":"libs/atoms/src/atoms/spec.py","lines":"128-148","note":"Spec.replay_from definition for suffix replay.","quote":"    def replay_from(\n        self, state: dict[str, Any], payloads: Iterable[dict[str, Any]]\n    ) -\u003e dict[str, Any]:\n        \"\"\"Suffix replay: continue folding from an existing ``state``.\n\n        Copies ``state`` ONCE (deep, as ``apply()`` does) and then mutates that\n        copy across every payload — the per-payload cost of ``replay()`` with\n        the input-purity of ``apply()``. Valid only when the fold replay order\n        is append order, so that a suffix of the receipt stream can be applied\n        to the state folded from its prefix.\n\n        The single deep copy is load-bearing for callers that keep a long-lived\n        checkpoint (``engine.handle``): the input ``state`` is never mutated, so\n        it may stay shared with an already-published snapshot.\n        \"\"\"\n        fns = self._cached_fold_fns\n        new = copy.deepcopy(state)\n        for payload in payloads:\n            for fn in fns:\n                fn(new, payload)\n        return new"},{"file":"libs/engine/src/engine/handle.py","lines":"752-1340","note":"VertexHandle checkpoint machinery and state reconstruction methods.","quote":"class VertexHandle:\n    \"\"\"A held, recompilable vertex session whose source of truth stays SQLite.\n\n    Serializes ``refresh()`` and ``receive()`` under one lock and permits one\n    active change iterator. Snapshot values are immutable and may be handed to a\n    painter. Multiple independent subscriptions use independent handles.\n    \"\"\""},{"file":"benchmarks/characterize.py","lines":"206-224","note":"Benchmark arm probe_store touching ingest/append and store scan.","quote":"def probe_store(depth: int) -\u003e list[Sample]:\n    \"\"\"Raw SqliteStore append and full-scan cost at `depth` existing rows.\"\"\""},{"file":"benchmarks/characterize.py","lines":"242-320","note":"Benchmark arm probe_vertex_layers touching fold, receive (ingest), and cold open.","quote":"def probe_vertex_layers(depth: int, include_sdk: bool) -\u003e list[Sample]:\n    \"\"\"Engine and (when present) sdk probes against one vertex filled to `depth`."}],"not_covered":"None. Looked in all requested locations across engine, sdk, atoms, and benchmarks.","question":"Combined-read fold fork, sdk read path, combined-read callers, and KEEP-fence locations in explore/arrival-sliceC.","search_method":"git branch verification, find_by_name, grep_search, view_file"},"json_schema":{"$comment":"Explorer output contract. Shapes recon as LOCATION claims the arbiter can grep, not verdict claims the arbiter would have to trust. Pass with --output-format=json --json-schema=\u003cthis file\u003e; read the result at .structured_output.","type":"object","properties":{"question":{"type":"string","description":"The question this explorer was asked, restated in its own words. A restatement that drifts is the cheapest possible signal that the prompt did not arrive."},"answer":{"type":"string","enum":["found","partial","not_found","question_not_locatable"],"description":"question_not_locatable means the question asked for a judgment rather than a location; say so instead of guessing."},"locations":{"type":"array","description":"Every claim is a location. No claim without a file:line the arbiter can open.","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"file":{"type":"string","description":"Repo-relative path."},"lines":{"type":"string","description":"Line or range, e.g. \"142\" or \"140-168\"."},"quote":{"type":"string","description":"The exact source text at those lines, verbatim. This is what makes the citation checkable."},"note":{"type":"string","description":"What this location shows, in one sentence. Describe, do not evaluate."}},"required":["file","lines","quote","note"]}},"search_method":{"type":"string","description":"The exact commands run to find these (grep/rg/find invocations), so coverage can be judged."},"not_covered":{"type":"string","description":"Where you did not look, and why. A named gap is useful; an unnamed one is a