docs/scratch/arrival-sliceB/explore/e4-reanchor.json:1:{"conversation_id":"2db282a0-e243-49d9-936a-809e77e1e61e","status":"SUCCESS","response":"### 1. Verbatim Quote: `libs/engine/src/engine/jsonl_store.py` lines 140–170\n\n```python\n140: -----------------------------------------------------\n141: ``absorb_genesis`` and ``absorb_edit`` are append-shaped and run here per\n142: design:architecture/jsonl-declaration-ceremony-encoding: the base ceremonies\n143: reconcile first (``_sync_derived_state``), run every compare-and-swap check\n144: inside ``BEGIN IMMEDIATE`` *before* any log byte, then hand the assembled\n145: rows to the ``_ceremony_persist`` seam — which this class overrides to append\n146: the ceremony as ONE durable line (a plain fact line for one row, a\n147: ``\"t\":\"batch\"`` envelope for several; one line is the log's atomicity unit,\n148: so a torn ceremony is truncated whole and recovery can never expose a partial\n149: one), fsync, and stamp offset + counts before the commit. A refusal\n150: (``GenesisExists``/``NoGenesis``/``AmbiguousGenesis``/``StaleDeclarationHead``/\n151: ``ReservedKindViolation``/signing failures) rolls back with the log\n152: byte-identical to its pre-call state.\n153: \n154: ``reanchor`` is genuinely history-mutating — it rewrites sqlite rows the log\n155: keeps the originals of — and still refuses with\n156: :class:`JsonlCanonicalUnsupported` until the log-rewrite ceremony is\n157: designed. ``rebirth``/``compact`` live in ``libs/store`` and are detected,\n158: not refused (above).\n159: \"\"\"\n160: \n161: from __future__ import annotations\n162: \n163: import contextlib\n164: import itertools\n165: import logging\n166: import os\n167: import sqlite3\n168: from pathlib import Path\n169: from typing import Any, Generic, TypeVar\n170: \n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Definitions and Callers of `reanchor` across `libs/` and `apps/`\n\n#### Method and Function Definitions\n- [libs/engine/src/engine/sqlite_store.py:1675](file:///private